{{- /*
=============================================================================
configure-claude-theme — idempotent ~/.claude/settings.json theme patcher

Claude Code (Anthropic's terminal AI coding assistant) loads its theme
selection from ~/.claude/settings.json. The `theme` key accepts a built-in
preset name ("dark", "light", "dark-daltonized", "light-daltonized",
"dark-ansi", "light-ansi", "auto") or a custom theme reference of the form
"custom:<slug>" where <slug> is the filename in ~/.claude/themes/ without
the .json extension. Selecting the theme stores "custom:tokyo-night-moon"
here; the theme file itself is deployed as a plain chezmoi file target at
dot_claude/themes/tokyo-night-moon.json → ~/.claude/themes/tokyo-night-moon.json.

~/.claude/settings.json is NOT fully owned by the repo — Claude Code writes
runtime keys (hooks, permissions, env, statusLine, autoCompactEnabled) and
the user edits it interactively via /config. A templated file target would
clobber those keys; this jq merge preserves every existing field and only
sets the `theme` scalar to "custom:tokyo-night-moon".

Uses `run_onchange_before_` semantics:
  • `onchange_` runs only when THIS SCRIPT'S source content has changed
    (chezmoi state hash), so re-applies don't churn ~/.claude/settings.json's
    mtime once the patch is stable.
  • `before_` runs during step 4 of the application order, before file
    targets are written — matters because ~/.claude/settings.json is NOT
    a chezmoi-managed file; this script is the only writer for the `theme`
    key. The theme JSON file is written in step 5 as a normal chezmoi file
    target; the ordering here only matters relative to other run-scripts
    that might read this file's output.

No-op on a fresh machine where claude code has never been run (the
~/.claude/ dir won't exist yet — claude creates it on first launch). The
user runs `claude` once to initialize, then re-runs `chezmoi apply` to
apply the theme selection. Same friendly-fail-mode pattern AGENTS.md
describes for dot_zprofile on a machine where brew isn't installed yet.
=============================================================================
*/ -}}
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

CLAUDE_DIR="$HOME/.claude"
SETTINGS_FILE="$CLAUDE_DIR/settings.json"

# No-op if claude code has never been run (dir or settings file doesn't exist).
if [ ! -f "$SETTINGS_FILE" ]; then
  echo "==> Claude Code settings not found at $SETTINGS_FILE — claude not initialized yet."
  echo "    Run 'claude' once to initialize, then re-run 'chezmoi apply' to select the theme."
  exit 0
fi

echo "==> Selecting Tokyo Night Moon theme for Claude Code (~/.claude/settings.json)..."
tmp=$(mktemp)
jq --arg theme "custom:tokyo-night-moon" '.theme = $theme' "$SETTINGS_FILE" > "$tmp" && mv "$tmp" "$SETTINGS_FILE"
echo "    theme = custom:tokyo-night-moon (other keys preserved — hooks, permissions, env, etc.)"
{{- else -}}
{{- /* No-op on non-macOS. */ -}}
{{- end -}}